  "finite_blowdown_stack_theorem": {
    "essential_limitation": "Absence of every hidden negative curve is not supplied by the finite incidence stack.  Without a P-derived height bound, verified Cox-ring presentation, or a classification/root-exhaustion theorem, it is an infinite Hilbert-scheme union, not a finite algebraic condition.",
    "incidence_stack": "Each terminal P2 or Hirzebruch branch determines a finite Enriques/proximity diagram.  Its cluster space and the relative Hilbert/projective bundles for the finitely many pushed-down wall classes give a finite-type locally closed stack.",
    "nonemptiness": "After finite cohomology/base-change stratification, simultaneous effectivity, smoothness, irreducibility, incidence, |-K|=empty, and h0(-2K)=1 are finite polynomial open/closed conditions; over a fixed algebraically closed field their nonemptiness is an exact saturated-ideal question.",
    "statement": "For an exact full-nef strong-Coble carrier of a finite raw wall system, every curve contracted in a minimal-model sequence pulls back to a negative curve and therefore occurs among the input facets.  Contracting a (-1)-curve updates D.F to D.F+(D.E)(F.E) and K to K-E.  Rank drops at every step, so enumerating eligible facet sequences is finite and exhaustive among exact carriers."
  },
